  "_note": "Culture biome profiles (owner decisions 2026-10-04, game-design §12.13 C; docs/map-pipeline-design.md Addendum A). ground: the terrain shader's colours (map/terrain_view.gdshader; targets: docs/reference/biomes/, palette and materials, not layout): grass and dry patches on open land, forest floor and canopy (forests read as a canopy carpet from afar), rock on steep slopes, scree at the feet of the ranges, snow above snow_line metres (999 = none), dirt for passes, roads and settlements, sand on beaches, water for rivers. forest: density multiplier and the tree models (asset manifest nature.*, Quaternius Stylized Nature, weighted), their tint and scale [width, height]. A culture with no fitting tree model in the pack (desert palms, jungle giants) uses the closest one scaled until its procedural kit has its own. layout: the settlement layout style (map/sprawl.gd: grid, plaza, river, terraces, organic, stacks, cliff, camp, spires, crags, wild); every culture has its own procedural building kit (visuals/kits/cultures/culture_kit.gd, manifest ids kit.<culture>.<piece>). tint: stone/wall, roof/house and ruin multipliers (ruin is used for ruined pieces). map_color: the strategic map's Culture layer. Chaos and Hollow Dynasty profiles are post-V1; add them here as data.",
  "conversion": {
    "_note": "A region taken from another culture turns toward its new owner's profile: noticeable after noticeable_turns, very noticeable after very_turns, fully converted after full_turns (the value rises 1/full_turns per End Turn). Each building in the region that the owner completed after taking it adds per_building to the turn's progress. ruin_band: the share of the old culture's pieces shown as ruins just before they are replaced. PLACEHOLDER numbers.",
    "noticeable_turns": 3,
    "very_turns": 6,
    "full_turns": 9,
    "per_building": 0.03,
    "ruin_band": 0.3
  },
